Root cause:
The bug was caused by the `mCurPage` not being set to `null` immediately when the last page was popped, which could lead to inconsistencies in the current page state during transition animations. This resulted in the application potentially referencing an outdated or incorrect current page while the animation was still playing.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
mCurPage = prevPage;
```
```java
if (animated && mPageAnimator != null && !removedPage.onPopPageAnimation(removedPage, prevPage, hint)) {
```
```java
prevPage.getView().setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because `mCurPage` is not set to `null` immediately when the last page is popped. This means that during the transition animation, the application may still reference the outdated `mCurPage`, leading to inconsistencies in the current page state.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
mCurPage = prevPage;
```
```java
mContainerView.removeView(removedPage.getView());
```
Reason:
The fix involves setting `mCurPage` to `prevPage` immediately after removing the view of the `removedPage`. This ensures that the current page state is updated correctly, preventing any references to an outdated page during the transition animation.


